==============================================================================
1. Symbolic (SymPy)
==============================================================================
1a. (2/pi) elliptic_k(sin^2(theta0/2)) = 1 + theta0**2/16 + 11*theta0**4/3072 + 173*theta0**6/737280 + O(theta0**8)
1b. (2/pi) K(m) from term-by-term integration = 25*m**3/256 + 9*m**2/64 + m/4 + 1 + O(m^4)
    check against ((2n)!/(2^{2n} n!^2))^2: [1, 1/4, 9/64, 25/256] match = True
    substituted m = sin^2(theta0/2): 173*theta0**6/737280 + 11*theta0**4/3072 + theta0**2/16 + 1
1c. Lindstedt-Poincare: w2 = -1/8 ; T/T0 = epsilon**2/16 + 1 + O(eps^4)
    (eps and theta0 differ at O(eps^3), which changes T/T0 only at O(theta0^4))

a (from 1a) = 1/16  (from 1b) = 1/16  (from 1c) = 1/16
theta0^4 coefficient (1a) = 11/3072  (1b) = 11/3072
theta0^6 coefficient (1a) = 173/737280  (1b, needs m^3 term, included) = 173/737280
LaTeX:  T = T_0\left(1 + \frac{\theta_{0}^{2}}{16} + \frac{11 \theta_{0}^{4}}{3072} + \frac{173 \theta_{0}^{6}}{737280} + O(\theta_0^{8})\right)
LaTeX:  a = \frac{1}{16}
LaTeX:  \frac{2}{\pi}K(m) = 1 + \frac{m}{4} + \frac{9 m^{2}}{64} + \frac{25 m^{3}}{256} + O(m^4)

