theta0 = pi/2: (2/pi)K = 1.180340599016096226, Gamma(1/4)^2/(2 pi^(3/2)) = 1.180340599016096226, ODE = 1.180340599016107
theta0 = 1e-8: T/T0 - 1 = 6.25e-18 (expected theta0^2/16 = 6.25e-18)
T/T0 increasing on (0, pi): True
theta0 = pi - 1e-6: T/T0 = 10.119041 (diverges logarithmically as theta0 -> pi; (2/pi) ln(8/(pi - theta0)) = 10.119041)
Convention trap at theta0 = 0.01: ellipk(k) instead of ellipk(k^2) gives (T/T0-1)/theta0^2 = 12.5352 instead of 0.062500
Dimensions: T0 = 2 pi sqrt(L/g) carries time; T/T0 is a function of the angle theta0 only, so a is a pure number (per rad^2).
